;;
;; Who is in a role today, for every ticket at once.
;;
;; A definition says which roles a process HAS; this says who is in one.
;; Membership is organisation state, not a rule of the process — with the
;; definition as the only source, a hire or a departure would be a
;; version bump, and every in-flight ticket would need migrating before
;; it took effect. Resolving outside the pin means a change here lands on
;; everything already deriving, immediately.
;;
;; That is also what lets the definitions in processes/ ship with empty
;; members: they are the same processes anyone else can adopt, and this
;; file is the part that is ours. A role absent here keeps whatever its
;; definition declares.
{:triager    {:members ["seb"]}
 :billing    {:members ["billing"]}
 :maintainer {:members ["seb"]}}
